# Corpus unit semantic-self-consistency/C05 — gap (both policy-mandatory correlation CQs unmet)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/semantic-self-consistency.yaml C05 (descriptive, statistical_correlation;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: average reasoning-chain sequence length positively correlates with
# the average accuracy increase from the semantic methods, over the 15 model-dataset pairs of
# Table 3.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * statistical_correlation family -> statistical_correlation(X, Y, S, Exp), conclusion
#     correlated(X, Y, S) with X = avg_seq_length, Y = accuracy_increase, S = model_dataset_pairs.
#   * Both mandatory corpus-v1 CQs are annotated unmet-gap, so the argument is incomplete: it is
#     declared as a located hole with `open significance` and `open independence` (lowering
#     re-done for issue #15 under lara-core@0.3), and the claim lands `gap` on empty complete
#     support: significance <- CQ1 (Table 3's note asserts "positive correlation observed" but no
#     coefficient or test appears anywhere; recomputed r = 0.242, t ~ 0.90, not significant at n =
#     15); independence <- CQ2 (5 models x 3 datasets, same model contributes 3 correlated points,
#     unaddressed). No mandatory CQ is met, so only the premise leaf is kept. The optional
#     confound CQ (instruction-tuning third variable) is also unmet; optional, no status effect.
#   * Borderline (annotation `uncertain: true`): with r = 0.242 n.s. one could read the missing
#     test as an unmet-defeater, but the claim's own falsification criterion is sign-based ("no
#     positive correlation") and the sign is positive, so the claim is under-established, not
#     defeated -> gap, not defeated. This is C05's own (avg_seq_length, accuracy_increase) pair;
#     C06's BLEU pair is a different (X, Y) in its own unit, so no contrary/rebut edge is forced
#     here. The recomputed r and the mechanism rider live in nl. Dead ends N06/N07/N12 are
#     rejected design alternatives -- no attacks.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact semantic-self-consistency at sha256:970cd14ac108
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not complete at corpus-v1's evidential bar -----------------

claim c05
  nl      = "Average reasoning-chain sequence length positively correlates with the average accuracy increase from the semantic methods over the 15 model-dataset pairs of Table 3 (recomputed Pearson r ~= 0.242, not significant at n = 15)"
  formal  = correlated(avg_seq_length, accuracy_increase, model_dataset_pairs)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaf is present ... ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the Table 3 (seq_length, accuracy_increase) pairs and the asserted positive-
# trend note, folded into refs (including the long-sequence negative-gain counter-cell).
leaf e1 : reports(e04, correlation(avg_seq_length, accuracy_increase, model_dataset_pairs, present))
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C05, evidence/tables/table3_sequence_length_bleu.md, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N11]

# --- ... but the argument is incomplete (a located hole) ----------------------------------------

# significance (no coefficient or test reported) and independence (5 models x 3 datasets, the
# same model contributes 3 points) are open and mandatory, so a1 is a hole; the optional
# confound_control (instruction-tuning third variable) is open too.
arg a1 : supports(c05) by statistical_correlation(avg_seq_length, accuracy_increase, model_dataset_pairs, e04)
  open significance
  open independence
  open confound_control

status c05

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments (the hole is not a node).
# Located hole: a1, open obligations [significance, independence]; it sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c05 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8;
#          the located hole is reported in `holes`, not counted as support)
